{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a captivating film that delves into the creation and meteoric rise of facebook, while also exploring the complex and often controversial personal relationships of its founder mark zuckerberg. the movie begins by establishing zuckerberg as a socially awkward yet brilliant computer science student at harvard university. his coding skills and determination are portrayed through a series of scenes that highlight his ability to connect people in new and innovative ways.\n\none of the film's strongest aspects is its compelling portrayal of zuckerberg's interactions with classmates edwardo savarin, cameron winklevoss, and divya narendra, who claim he stole their idea for a social networking site. these conflicts not only add tension to the narrative but also provide insight into the legal and ethical issues surrounding the early days of facebook.\n\nthe performances in the social network are exceptional. jesse Eisenberg delivers a nuanced portrayal of zuckerberg, capturing both his brilliance and his flaws. andrew garfield, as winklevoss, and josh hartnett, as savarin, also give strong performances that add depth to their characters. the film uses flashbacks and dialogue-driven scenes effectively to move the story forward and keep the audience engaged.\n\nvisually, the social network is impressive. the film employs a modern, sleek style that complements the story's focus on technology and innovation. the use of color and lighting is particularly striking, with cool tones often used to convey the sterile, digital world that zuckerberg inhabits.\n\nthe social network succeeds in balancing the personal and professional aspects of its subject matter. it offers a glimpse into the world of silicon valley and the tech startup culture, while also exploring themes of friendship, rivalry, and the price of success. the film's script is sharp and witty, with dialogue that often feels like it could have been taken directly from a real-life tech conference or a late-night coding session.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-crafted, thought-provoking movie that provides an engaging look at the birth of facebook and the man behind it. it's a film that will appeal to fans of biographical dramas and anyone interested in the tech industry, as well as those who appreciate strong performances and compelling storytelling. the movie's exploration of ambition, innovation, and the human cost of achieving success makes it a relevant and powerful watch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.16252879798412323}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.00573216937482357}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -0.00048065552255138755}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.1040261834859848}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.17000918090343475}, {"token": " captivating", "logprob": -0.9908629059791565}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.5125409364700317}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.10917671024799347}, {"token": " delves", "logprob": -0.36758914589881897}, {"token": " into", "logprob": -0.05003853887319565}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0010063351364806294}, {"token": " creation", "logprob": -2.0596113204956055}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.6368384957313538}, {"token": " met", "logprob": -1.1274445056915283}, {"token": "e", "logprob": -0.0001565095444675535}, {"token": "oric", "logprob": -6.198863957251888e-06}, {"token": " rise", "logprob": -0.00019453064305707812}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0002165798214264214}, {"token": " face", "logprob": -0.003854228649288416}, {"token": "book", "logprob": -5.566918844124302e-05}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.5835914611816406}, {"token": " while", "logprob": -4.136625289916992}, {"token": " also", "logprob": -0.08486556261777878}, {"token": " exploring", "logprob": -0.3455459177494049}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.052782800048589706}, {"token": " complex", "logprob": -